# Git Workflow

## Branch Protection

- **Never push directly to `main`** — all changes must go through a pull request
- A pre-push hook enforces this locally when installed; GitHub branch protection enforces it remotely
- If you need to commit, always create a feature branch first

## Branch Naming

- Use descriptive branch names: `<scope>-<feature>` (e.g., `web-test-catalog-home`, `fix-login-redirect`)
- Keep branch names lowercase with hyphens

## Workflow

1. Create a feature branch from `main`: `git checkout -b <branch-name>`
2. Make commits on the feature branch (pre-commit hook runs checks)
3. Push the branch: `git push -u origin <branch-name>`
4. Create a PR against `main`
5. Squash and merge after review and CI passes

## Hooks

- **pre-commit**: Runs unit tests and production build when webapp files change; YAML/markdown lint when those files change
- Install hooks: `./utils/setup-hooks.sh`
